tates and internationally. It operates through Texas Roadhouse, Bubba's 33, and Others segments. The company's restaurants offer seasoned and aged steaks, ribs, seafood, chicken, pork chops, pulled pork, and vegetable plates, as well as an assortment of hamburgers, salads, and sandwiches; and pizza, wings, and various appetizers and dinner entr\u00e9es. The company also operates and franchises restaurants under the Texas Roadhouse, Bubba's 33, and Jaggers brands. Texas Roadhouse, Inc. was founded in 1993 and is based in Louisville, Kentucky.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Gerald L. Morgan | CEO & Executive Vice Chairman | Age 64 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 101K people. Revenue per employee of $58K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $3K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $473 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 41\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Texas Roadhouse, Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $12.2B market cap on $5.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 32% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 24-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $342M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.80\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 41% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.40866325536527637},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headline